<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 1.9 pct in Oct 1-10 - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 1.9 pct in Oct 1-10 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 2.28 billion zlotys, or 1.9 percent, between October 1-10 to 125.51 billion zlotys, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>This followed a 1.2 percent rise in September.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		 OCTOBER 1-10  SEPTEMBER  OCT 95</p>
<p>  change (pct)				1.9	  1.2	 3.0</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   125.51     123.23     97.45</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	22.47	22.39     20.84</p>
<p>  National currency		     103.05     100.84     76.61</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    23.28	23.02     18.52</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    71.20	70.57     53.48</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
